        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 43.9" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="569" ed="#liebermann"/>Sustinere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="s" target="#Hn_43-9.lnote.oe.s"/> tamen debet homo dominum suum, si faciat ei contumeliam uel iniuriam eiusmodi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Hn_43-9.lnote.oe.32"/>, in werra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Hn_43-9.lnote.oe.33"/> triginta dies, in pace unum annum et unum diem; et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Hn_43-9.lnote.oe.34"/> interim priuate per<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Hn_43-9.lnote.oe.35"/> compares, per uicinos, <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Hn_43-9.lnote.oe.36"/>per domesticos et extraneos per leges<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Hn_43-9.lnote.oe.37"/> require(ret<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#Hn_43-9.lnote.oe.38"/>) eum de recto.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 569 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_43-9.lnote.oe.s" n="s" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">569</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 83, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. 83, 1</seg></note>
